ds of computational linguistics and probability, an n-gram is a contiguous sequence of n items from a given sequence of text or speech. The items can be phonemes, syllables, letters, words or base pairs according to the application. The n-grams typically are collected from a text or speech corpus. When the items are words, n-grams may also be called shingles.[1]  An n-gram of size 1 is referred to as a \"unigram\"; size 2 is a \"bigram\" (or, less commonly, a \"digram\"); size 3 is a \"trigram\". Larger sizes are sometimes referred to by the value of n, e.g., \"four-gram\", \"five-gram\", and so on.","topics":[],"score":212097,"global_rank":273410},{"name":"xinghai-zhang/Mhacks6","owner":"xinghai-zhang","html_url":"https://github.com/xinghai-zhang/Mhacks6","stars":1,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"Automatically generates powerpoint from news articles on the web.","topics":[],"score":212072,"global_rank":273454},{"name":"torontodeveloper/realtor-django","owner":"torontodeveloper","html_url":"https://github.com/torontodeveloper/realtor-django","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"Realtor website using Django","topics":[],"score":212067,"global_rank":273488},{"name":"Pritiks23/persistant-memory","owner":"Pritiks23","html_url":"https://github.com/Pritiks23/persistant-memory","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":null,"topics":[],"score":212067,"global_rank":273490},{"name":"Pritiks23/jstforme","owner":"Pritiks23","html_url":"https://github.com/Pritiks23/jstforme","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":null,"topics":[],"score":212067,"global_rank":273491},{"name":"liliiakryvelova/movie-recommendation-system","owner":"liliiakryvelova","html_url":"https://github.com/liliiakryvelova/movie-recommendation-system","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":null,"topics":[],"score":212067